    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/admin/ontologies/2025/7/AZD">
        <dc:creator>Subhashis Das</dc:creator>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2025-09-02T17:30:00+02:00</dc:date>
        <dc:title>Alzheimer’s Disease Ontology (AZD)</dc:title>
        <rdfs:comment>The Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Ontology (AZDOnto) is a specialized knowledge representation framework developed to support the integration and analysis of clinical data related to Alzheimer&apos;s disease (AD). This ontology is primarily designed to leverage Electronic Health Record (EHR) data, providing a standardized structure for the representation of patient information. The AZDOnto facilitates the effective integration of data from a variety of sources, enabling clinicians, researchers, and data scientists to gain insights into the clinical, genetic, and therapeutic aspects of Alzheimer&apos;s disease.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


